activities.content:
A parameterized constructor is simply a constructor that has a parameter list inside its parentheses.

### Syntax Blueprint:
```java
class Student {
    String name;
    int age;

    // Parameterized constructor: accepts custom data at birth
    Student(String sName, int sAge) {
        name = sName; // Store parameter value into instance field
        age = sAge;
    }
}
```

### Calling the Parameterized Constructor:
```java
// Values "Rahul" and 20 are passed directly into the constructor
Student s1 = new Student("Rahul", 20);
Student s2 = new Student("Priya", 21);
```

### Visual Execution Tracing:
```text
Student s1 = new Student("Rahul", 20);
        │
        ├─► 1. 'new' creates empty Student in memory
        ├─► 2. Arguments "Rahul" and 20 are copied into parameters (sName, sAge)
        ├─► 3. Constructor assigns: name = sName ("Rahul")
        ├─► 4. Constructor assigns: age = sAge (20)
        └─► 5. Complete, fully-formed student reference is assigned to s1
```

### Why This Is Clean Engineering:
Instead of writing 4 separate lines of code for every object (`new`, `s.name = ...`, `s.age = ...`, `s.course = ...`), we initialize everything in a single, atomic line of code!

